    "rawContent": "---\nname: llm-cli\ndescription: Parallel LLM CLI execution with context support\ncategory: ai-llm\ntriggers:\n  - /llm-cli\naliases:\n  - /llm-cli\n\nsuggest:\n  - /llm-route\n  - /llm-health\n  - /nse\n---\n\n# LLM CLI\n\nParallel LLM CLI execution with context support.\n\n## Purpose\n\nParallel LLM CLI execution with context support.\n\n## Project Context\n\n### Constitution/Constraints\n- Evidence-first: Use LLM output faithfully, don't fabricate findings\n- Safety: Never send secrets or environment files intentionally\n\n### Technical Context\n- Uses: `P:/__csf/src/features/commands/co/llm_cli.py`\n- Supports multiple providers: qwen, gemini, codex\n- Auto-context loading from session history available\n\n### Architecture Alignment\n- Integrates with `/llm-route` for provider routing\n- Works with `/llm-health` for provider status\n- Integrates with `/nse` for Next Step Engine\n\n## Your Workflow\n\nWhen `/llm-cli` is invoked:\n1. Parse prompt and flags (--auto-context, --context, provider flags)\n2. Execute parallel LLM calls\n3. Return combined results with attribution\n\n## Validation Rules\n\n### Safety & Constraints\n- Never send secrets or environment files intentionally (.env, keys, tokens)\n- Avoid including lockfiles or large binaries unless task requires them\n- Don't fabricate findings about files LLM did not see\n- Use repo-relative paths only (don't invent files)\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n/llm-cli \"explain recursion\"\n/llm-cli \"what did I just ask?\" --auto-context\n/llm-cli \"debug this\" --qwen-only\n```\n\n## Flags\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `--auto-context` | Load latest session history |\n| `--context <id>` | Load specific session |\n| `--qwen-only` | Run only Qwen |\n| `--gemini-only` | Run only Gemini |\n| `--codex-only` | Run only Codex |\n\n## Implementation\n\nUses: `P:/__csf/src/features/commands/co/llm_cli.py`\n"
