  "/test": {
    "id": "/test",
    "name": "test",
    "description": "Test coverage and gap analysis - what tests exist, what's missing, and what to add",
    "category": "testing",
    "filePath": "P:\\.claude\\skills\\test\\SKILL.md",
    "directives": "",
    "doNot": [],
    "defaultArgs": "",
    "examples": [],
    "summary": "Test coverage and gap analysis - what tests exist, what's missing, and what to add",
    "howToUse": "",
    "suggest": [
      "/comply",
      "/qa",
      "/bug-hunt"
    ],
    "rawContent": "---\nname: test\ndescription: Test coverage and gap analysis - what tests exist, what's missing, and what to add\ncategory: testing\ntriggers:\n  - /test\n  - /tests\n  - \"test coverage\"\n  - \"what's tested\"\n  - \"test gaps\"\n  - \"coverage report\"\n  - \"what tests do I need\"\naliases:\n  - /test\n\nsuggest:\n  - /comply\n  - /qa\n  - /bug-hunt\n---\n\n# /test - Test Coverage & Gap Analysis\n\n## Purpose\n\nVisibility into what tests exist, what's missing, and what should be added next. Answers questions TDD doesn't: \"What tests do I have?\", \"What am I missing?\", \"What edge cases aren't tested?\"\n\n## Project Context\n\n### Constitution / Constraints\n- **Solo-dev constraints apply** (CLAUDE.md)\n- **Evidence-based**: Map coverage to actual code paths, don't assume\n- **TDD complement**: Use /test to see gaps, /tdd to write missing tests\n- **Quality > quantity**: High coverage of wrong tests still fails\n\n### Technical Context\n- **Test discovery**: Find test files via patterns (test_*.py, *_integration.py)\n- **Classification**: Unit, Integration, Edge Case, Error Path, Regression\n- **Coverage analysis**: Map code components to test coverage\n- **Output format**: Structured report with gaps and prioritized recommendations\n\n### Architecture Alignment\n- Integrates with /tdd (write tests), /verify (run tests), /qa (certify feature)\n- Links to /test-bisect (regression hunting), /bug-hunt (find bugs)\n- Part of testing ecosystem\n\n## Your Workflow\n\n1. **DISCOVER TESTS** \u2014 Find all test files related to target\n2. **CLASSIFY TESTS** \u2014 Categorize as Unit, Integration, Edge Case, Error Path, Regression\n3. **ANALYZE COVERAGE** \u2014 Map code components to test coverage\n4. **IDENTIFY GAPS** \u2014 Find missing functions, edge cases, error paths\n5. **GENERATE REPORT** \u2014 Structured coverage report with metrics\n6. **RECOMMEND ACTIONS** \u2014 Prioritized list of missing tests with DUF-style options\n\n## Validation Rules\n\n- **Before reporting coverage**: Actually discover and read test files\n- **Before claiming gaps**: Verify code component exists and has no test\n- **Before recommending**: Prioritize by risk (critical > important > nice-to-have)\n- **Evidence required**: Cite actual test file names and function names\n\n### Prohibited Actions\n- Replacing /tdd (use /test to see gaps, /tdd to write)\n- Reporting coverage without mapping to actual code paths\n- Ignoring edge cases (where bugs hide)\n- Assuming coverage = quality\n\n## Existing Purpose\n\nAnswer questions that TDD doesn't:\n- \"What tests do I have?\"\n- \"What am I missing?\"\n- \"Do I have integration tests?\"\n- \"What % of my code is covered?\"\n- \"What edge cases aren't tested?\"\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n/test \"notification_queue.py\"\n/test \"What's my test coverage?\"\n/test \"Am I missing integration tests?\"\n```\n\n## The Analysis Framework\n\n### 1. Discover Tests\n\nFind all test files related to the target:\n- Unit test files: `tests/test_<module>.py`\n- Integration test files: `tests/*_integration.py`, `tests/integration/`\n- Test methods within files: `def test_*`\n\n### 2. Classify Tests\n\n| Type | Pattern | Example |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| **Unit** | `test_<function>()` - single function/unit | `test_mark_cleared()` |\n| **Integration** | `test_*_integration()`, `test_*_flow()` | `test_stop_hook_flow()` |\n| **Edge Case** | `test_*edge*`, `test_*boundary*` | `test_empty_input()` |\n| **Error Path** | `test_*error*`, `test_*invalid*` | `test_corrupted_json()` |\n| **Regression** | `test_*regression*`, `test_bisect` | `test_reproduce_bug_123()` |\n\n### 3. Analyze Coverage\n\nMap code components to test coverage:\n\n| Component | Tests | Coverage |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Function `mark_cleared()` | \u2705 `test_mark_cleared_blocks_add` | Covered |\n| Function `_get_cleared_time()` | \u274c None | **MISSING** |\n| Corrupted JSON handling | \u274c None | **MISSING** |\n| Concurrent access | \u274c None | **MISSING** |\n\n### 4. Generate Action Items\n\n```\n**1** - Add test for [missing function]\n**2** - Add edge case test for [condition]\n**3** - Add error path test for [exception]\n**4** - Add integration test for [flow]\n**5** - /tdd (use TDD to implement all tests)\n**6** - All (implement all)\n**7** - None (skip)\n```\n\n## Response Format\n\n```\n## Test Coverage Report: [target]\n\n### Test Files Found\n- `tests/test_notification_queue.py` (6 tests)\n- `tests/test_router_integration.py` (2 tests)\n\n### Coverage by Type\n\n#### Unit Tests\n\u2705 `test_mark_cleared_blocks_add`\n\u2705 `test_cleared_state_expires`\n\u2705 `test_mark_cleared_only_affects_specific_type`\n\u274c **MISSING**: `test_get_cleared_time()`\n\u274c **MISSING**: `test_set_cleared_time()`\n\n#### Integration Tests\n\u2705 `test_router_clears_and_marks`\n\u274c **MISSING**: Stop hook timing test\n\u274c **MISSING**: Multi-terminal race condition\n\n#### Edge Cases\n\u274c **MISSING**: Empty state file\n\u274c **MISSING**: Future timestamp\n\u274c **MISSING**: Corrupted JSON\n\n#### Error Paths\n\u274c **MISSING**: Invalid JSON format\n\u274c **MISSING**: File permission denied\n\n### Coverage Summary\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Functions tested | 3/7 (43%) |\n| Edge cases covered | 0/4 (0%) |\n| Error paths covered | 0/2 (0%) |\n| **Overall Coverage** | **~25%** |\n\n### Gaps Identified\n1. `_get_cleared_time()` - No direct tests\n2. `_set_cleared_time()` - No direct tests\n3. No corrupted JSON recovery test\n4. No concurrent access test\n5. No timezone edge cases\n\n### Recommendations\n\n**Priority 1 - Critical Gaps:**\n**1** - Add corrupted JSON test (data safety)\n**2** - Add concurrent access test (multi-terminal safety)\n\n**Priority 2 - Important Gaps:**\n**3** - Add test for `_get_cleared_time()`\n**4** - Add test for `_set_cleared_time()`\n\n**Priority 3 - Nice to Have:**\n**5** - Add timezone edge case tests\n**6** - Add permission denied test\n\n**Options:**\n**5** - /tdd (implement all using TDD workflow)\n**6** - All (implement all recommendations)\n**7** - None (skip - current coverage is acceptable)\n```\n\n## When to Use\n\n| Situation | Tool |\n|-----------|------|\n| Writing new code | `/tdd` (write tests first) |\n| Checking what exists | `/test` (coverage report) |\n| Pre-commit verification | `/verify` (run tests) |\n| Finding test gaps | `/test` (gap analysis) |\n| Feature certification | `/qa` (full test suite) |\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Don't | Do Instead |\n|-------|-------------|\n| Replace `/tdd` | Use `/test` to see what's missing, `/tdd` to write |\n| Test coverage without context | Always map coverage to actual code paths |\n| Ignore edge cases | They're where bugs hide |\n| Assume coverage = quality | High coverage of wrong tests still fails |\n\n## Related Commands\n\n- **`/tdd`** - Test-Driven Development workflow\n- **`/verify`** - Run tests and check regressions\n- **`/qa`** - Feature certification with full test suite\n- **`/test-bisect`** - Regression hunting with git bisect\n\n## Recommended Workflow\n\n```\n/test \u2192 see gaps \u2192 /tdd (write missing tests) \u2192 /verify (run)\n```\n\n---\n\n**Version:** 1.0.0\n**Created:** 2026-01-16\n"
  },
