  "/workflow": {
    "id": "/workflow",
    "name": "workflow",
    "description": "Create, manage, and execute automated workflows with multi-step sequences and conditional branching",
    "category": "workflow",
    "filePath": "P:\\.claude\\skills\\workflow\\SKILL.md",
    "directives": "",
    "doNot": [],
    "defaultArgs": "",
    "examples": [],
    "summary": "Create, manage, and execute automated workflows with multi-step sequences and conditional branching",
    "howToUse": "",
    "suggest": [
      "/cwo",
      "/nse",
      "/build"
    ],
    "rawContent": "---\nname: workflow\ndescription: Create, manage, and execute automated workflows with multi-step sequences and conditional branching\ncategory: workflow\ntriggers:\n  - /workflow\naliases:\n  - /workflow\n\nsuggest:\n  - /cwo\n  - /nse\n  - /build\n---\n\n# Workflow Management Command\n\nCreate, manage, and execute automated workflows with multi-step sequences, conditional branching, and error recovery.\n\n## Project Context\n\n### Constitution / Constraints\n- Solo-dev constraint: Practical workflow automation, not enterprise orchestration\n- Evidence-first: Verify workflow execution results\n\n### Technical Context\n- Workflow types: Sequential, Conditional Branching, Parallel Execution, Error Recovery\n- Step types: Command, Script, Condition, Delay, Webhook, Notification\n- Templates: Code Review, Deployment, Testing, Security Scan\n\n### Architecture Alignment\n- Workflow engine: Multi-step automation with state management\n- Template system: Reusable workflow patterns\n\n## Your Workflow\n1. Receive workflow command (create, list, execute, status, cancel, metrics)\n2. Parse arguments and options\n3. Execute workflow operation\n4. Display results or status\n\n## Validation Rules\n### Prohibited Actions\n- Do NOT create always-running daemons\n- Do NOT use enterprise orchestration patterns\n\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\n/workflow                           # Show workflow help\n/workflow create                    # Create workflow interactively\n/workflow list                      # List all workflows\n/workflow templates                 # List available templates\n/workflow execute <workflow_id>     # Execute a workflow\n/workflow status <execution_id>     # Check execution status\n/workflow cancel <execution_id>     # Cancel execution\n/workflow metrics                    # Show engine metrics\n```\n\n## Examples\n\n```bash\n# Create an interactive workflow\n/workflow create\n\n# List available workflows\n/workflow list\n\n# Execute a code review workflow\n/workflow execute abc123-def456\n\n# Check execution status\n/workflow status exec-789xyz\n\n# Cancel running execution\n/workflow cancel exec-789xyz\n\n# Show workflow metrics\n/workflow metrics\n\n# Create workflow from template\n/workflow from-template code_review \"My Code Review\" \"Personal code review workflow\"\n```\n\n## Features\n\n### Workflow Types\n- **Sequential Workflows**: Step-by-step execution\n- **Conditional Branching**: If/else logic and switch cases\n- **Parallel Execution**: Multiple steps running simultaneously\n- **Error Recovery**: Automatic retries and fallback procedures\n\n### Step Types\n- **Command**: Execute system commands or CLI tools\n- **Script**: Run Python scripts with context access\n- **Condition**: Evaluate expressions for branching\n- **Delay**: Pause execution for specified time\n- **Webhook**: Call external APIs\n- **Notification**: Send alerts and updates\n\n### Templates\n- **Code Review**: Automated testing and review workflow\n- **Deployment**: Multi-stage deployment with rollbacks\n- **Testing**: Comprehensive test suite execution\n- **Security Scan**: Automated security analysis\n"
  },
